 p('Each trip has a longitude/latitude/timestamp track, a longitude/latitude node table, directed arcs whose IDs are zero-based row numbers, and an ordered reference arc sequence. The reference sequence is not an observation-by-observation target. Arc IDs cannot be learned as global classes across different trip graphs.')
 p('The audit found no invalid or missing GPS rows in these development partitions. Training contains 1,216 gaps over five seconds, with a longest gap of 153,064 seconds; student testing contains 44, with a maximum of 210 seconds. About 96.50% and 98.62% of successive intervals are exactly one second. Directed reference routes have 13 and one adjacency breaks respectively. These observations motivate segment-aware features and explicit route restarts.')
 p('Preprocessing validates coordinates, timestamps, directed endpoints and reference IDs; sorts timestamps stably; removes duplicate timestamps; preserves original row IDs; and marks gaps and original-row discontinuities. Undefined motion is retained as unknown, not fabricated. Haversine distance is used for routing lengths; local equirectangular coordinates support metre-scale candidate projection.')
