 p('All directed arc segments within 50 metres form an observation candidate set. The midpoint search is length-banded and bounded by the triangle inequality, then exact segment distance filters the results. Long arcs are not missed simply because their midpoint is far away. Original arc IDs and fractions along arcs are preserved.')
 table(['Feature group','Purpose'],[['Distance and proximity','Perpendicular distance, log proximity rank, distance above best, and relative distance separate near and far roads.'],['Directed geometry','Along-arc fraction, log arc length, endpoint flags distinguish middle-of-road and junction behaviour.'],['Motion and ambiguity','Centred six-sample GPS heading compared with directed arc bearing, absolute sine difference, known-heading flag, log speed, and log candidate count provide direction and local ambiguity.']], [135,355])
 p('The 13 features contain no route labels, reference steps, trip IDs, arc IDs, absolute location or timestamps. Direction is estimated within continuous GPS segments; displacement below three metres is marked unknown. The centred window uses future GPS samples, making this an offline trip processor rather than a causal streaming predictor. Missing candidates remain missing predictions.')
