 p('Supervised targets come from monotone alignment to ordered reference-route occurrences within 75 metres, with a 75-metre unmatched cost and a three-metre ambiguity margin. Repeated arcs retain separate occurrences. Ambiguous and unmatched observations are excluded from supervised fitting. If the positive reference arc is outside the candidate set, the entire observation candidate group is excluded from binary fitting. These labels are estimates and can bias reported accuracy towards easy observations.')
 p('Observation top-1 accuracy includes candidate misses as errors among all aligned observations. Binary candidate F1/log loss use aligned observations whose positive arc exists. Both denominators and excluded counts are retained; the two metric families must not be interchanged.')
