 p('The full search record is in search_trials.csv and search.sqlite3; selected parameters are in tuning.json. Best-so-far search progress is an actual measured optimisation trace. Search scores can rise while separate development results stay flat or deteriorate. A tuned model is not assumed to be better until the held-out results support that statement.')
 page();heading('5. HMM and Viterbi route reconstruction')
 p('Hidden states are candidate positions (directed arc ID and fraction along that arc) for each GPS observation. Emission log scores are log(max(P(match), 1e-12)) from the selected classifier. Candidate membership and IDs remain keyed to their observation. Normalising emissions within an observation would add a state-independent constant and leave an uninterrupted path ranking unchanged.')
 p('A transition uses directed shortest-path road distance between candidate positions, including partial first and last arcs. Its log potential is -abs(road distance - GPS displacement)/beta. The search cutoff is max(GPS displacement, 65 m/s times the sample interval) plus 100 metres. It bounds shortest-path searches and is not a strict physical speed limit when GPS itself jumps. A training-selected same-arc jitter tolerance can treat a small decrease in projected offset as zero road movement: this models noisy GPS position without adding a reverse road edge. Impossible directed paths have no valid transition. This is an HMM-style log-potential decoder; transition terms are not claimed to be a calibrated physical generative distribution.')
 p('The recurrence is D_t(j) = emission_t(j) + max_i[D_(t-1)(i) + transition(i,j)]. Backpointers recover the best candidate sequence and intermediate graph arcs. Empty candidate sets return missing predictions and end the segment. Long timestamp gaps, original-row breaks and layers without a valid transition restart a segment. No unsupported line is drawn between disconnected segments.')
 p('Training-only calibration: a fresh classifier is fitted to two training folds, excluding the entire third fold. Four deterministic size-spread trips from that excluded fold score a six-setting beta/jitter grid with a five-second gap threshold. The selection objective is aligned-observation accuracy, with fewer route segments breaking exact ties. This avoids calibrating the decoder on a classifier that has already seen the calibration trips.')
 p('Selected decoder parameters: '+json.dumps(decoder['parameters'])+'. Calibration trip IDs: '+', '.join(decoder['calibration_trips'])+'. The calibration accuracy is '+pct(decoder['holdout_accuracy'])+'; it is a tuning score, not a final estimate.')
